   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Standing on the Moon** (1 review): Bobby's Standing on the Moon is marred on tape by a talker with an annoying laugh nearby [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Crowd 1st Set Intro & Tuning**: rare: 6 archived performances [7]\n- **Crowd 1st Set Intro & Tuning**: rare: 6 archived performances [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2024-08-10.Cancun_Mike** (recommended): source not stated; 24 songs; 180 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **deadco2024-08-10**: source not stated; 19 songs; 178 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [2]. Said about its sound: Clean recording with good clarity and definition; it captures some audience chatter at times; Fidelity is really nice throughout the recording [5][6]\n- **deadco2024-08-10.mv88**: source not stated; 20 songs; 176 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Crowd sing-alongs are audible, and the audience can be heard reacting to the Sphere visuals [5]\n- Billed as the Dead Forever finale at the Sphere; lineup was Weir, Hart, Mayer and Burbridge [1]\n- Recorded, mastered and uploaded by the Top Hat Crew, Big Jerry and Ladena Saxey [2]\n- Lineup listed: Weir on rhythm guitar, Hart percussion, Mayer lead guitar, Burbridge bass [3]\n- Reviewer attended the Aug. 1, 2 and 3 shows, where talkative fans were also noticed, as in many Sphere shows [5]\n- Reviewer thinks this might be the best show of the Sphere run [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2024-08-10.Cancun_Mike**: taped by Moe Reese; transferred by Eric Lugassy; source: Source: Church Audio CA-14 (omni) Bat2b custom modification > Stereo Breakout > Rode AI Micro > iPhone 14 Pro via Audio Share Application [1]\n- **deadco2024-08-10**: taped by Top Hat Crew (Big Jerry + Ladena Saxey); transferred by Top Hat Crew (Big Jerry); source: Microtech Gefell M21 DINa > nbob actives > Baby NBox > Sony PCM-A10 (24/48) [2]\n- **deadco2024-08-10.mv88**: taped by Neil Frost; transferred by Frostbyte; source: Shure MV88 ➔ iPhone [3]. Also: Shure MV88 into iPhone 15 Pro Max, MOTIV Video MOV, QuickTime m4a, Audacity tracking, FLAC, xACT tagging [3]",
